  "label": "User projected onto the child as the speaker of the text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the child, who is depicted as the speaker of the text 'my dad is the best at hide and seek'. The child's somber expression and central position in the image anchor the narrative, making the viewer identify with the child's perspective and experience of parental absence. The deictic 'my dad' in the text directly implicates the child as the speaker, creating a semiotic projection where the user sees themselves as the child in this scenario.",
